---

## Ⅰ. SPL — STUDY PATTERN LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   SPL
FULL NAME:      Study Pattern Language
LATIN:          Lingua Exemplarium Studii
ROLE:           Personal learning blueprints
FREQUENCY:      396 Hz (liberation — freeing the student's potential)
GLYPH:          𓇳 (sun — illumination)
```

### What SPL Governs
```
HOW A SPECIFIC STUDENT LEARNS:
    ├── Modalities — visual, auditory, kinesthetic, reading, social
    ├── Pacing — fast/slow, sprint/marathon, burst/steady
    ├── Repetition patterns — spaced repetition intervals, review curves
    ├── Scaffolding — what support structures the student needs
    ├── Attention patterns — focus duration, peak hours, fatigue curves
    └── Triggers — what engages, what bores, what overwhelms
```

### SPL Primitives
```
LEARNER(id, profile)                  — declare learner with profile
MODALITY(learner, type, strength)     — set learning modality strength
PACE(learner, pattern)                — set pacing pattern
REPETITION(concept, interval_curve)   — set spaced repetition schedule
SCAFFOLD(learner, support_type)       — add scaffolding
ATTENTION(learner, curve)             — model attention over time
TRIGGER(learner, stimulus, response)  — map engagement triggers
ADAPT(learner, feedback)              — adjust profile from feedback
```

---

## Ⅱ. EDL — EDUCATIONAL DOCTRINE LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   EDL
FULL NAME:      Educational Doctrine Language
LATIN:          Lingua Doctrinae Educationis
ROLE:           School/subject doctrine — what a system requires
FREQUENCY:      528 Hz (transformation — changing the student)
GLYPH:          𓏏 (bread — nourishment of knowledge)
```

### What EDL Governs
```
WHAT A SCHOOL/SYSTEM REQUIRES:
    ├── Standards — learning objectives, competency definitions
    ├── Competencies — measurable skills and knowledge
    ├── Graduation paths — sequences of requirements
    ├── Constraints — time limits, prerequisites, co-requisites
    ├── Assessment — how mastery is measured
    └── Curriculum — organized body of knowledge
```

### EDL Primitives
```
STANDARD(id, domain, level, description)   — declare learning standard
COMPETENCY(id, skills[], measurable_by)    — declare competency
GRADUATION(path_id, requirements[])        — declare graduation path
PREREQUISITE(course, required_before)      — set prerequisite
ASSESS(student, competency, method)        — define assessment
CURRICULUM(id, structure, sequence)        — declare curriculum
ALIGN(standard, competency)                — align standard to competency
ACCREDIT(program, authority)               — declare accreditation
```

---

## Ⅲ. PWL — PATHWAY LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   PWL
FULL NAME:      Pathway Language
LATIN:          Lingua Itineris
ROLE:           Life/education path language — multi-year trajectories
FREQUENCY:      639 Hz (connection — linking past to future)
GLYPH:          𓇼 (star path — celestial navigation)
```

### What PWL Governs
```
MULTI-YEAR TRAJECTORIES:
    ├── Courses — individual learning experiences
    ├── Projects — applied learning with deliverables
    ├── Colleges/institutions — where learning happens
    ├── Careers — professional destinations
    ├── Branching options — decision points and alternatives
    └── Milestones — markers of progress
```

### PWL Primitives
```
PATHWAY(id, start, destination, duration)  — declare a trajectory
BRANCH(pathway, condition, options[])      — declare branching point
MILESTONE(pathway, marker, criteria)       — declare milestone
COURSE(id, subject, duration, outcome)     — declare course
PROJECT(id, scope, deliverables)           — declare project
CAREER(id, field, entry_requirements)      — declare career destination
BRIDGE(pathway_a, pathway_b, transfer)     — declare pathway transfer
FORECAST(student, pathways[], fit_scores)  — predict pathway fit
```

---

## Ⅳ. TSL — TOOL SCAFFOLD LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   TSL
FULL NAME:      Tool Scaffold Language
LATIN:          Lingua Scaffoldi Instrumentorum
ROLE:           Personal tool-builder — designing custom tools for a student
FREQUENCY:      741 Hz (awakening — building capability)
GLYPH:          𓌻 (chisel — the tool that shapes)
```

### What TSL Governs
```
HOW THE SYSTEM DESIGNS CUSTOM TOOLS AROUND A STUDENT:
    ├── Flashcards — personalized spaced-repetition cards
    ├── Simulators — domain-specific practice environments
    ├── Planners — schedule and task management tools
    ├── Visualizers — concept maps, timelines, relationship graphs
    ├── Trackers — progress monitoring and streak systems
    └── Generators — problem/exercise generators calibrated to level
```

### TSL Primitives
```
TOOL(id, type, purpose, student_id)          — declare tool
SCAFFOLD_FOR(student, learning_gap, tool)    — match tool to gap
FLASHCARD_SET(topic, cards[], spacing)       — generate flashcard set
SIMULATOR(domain, rules, difficulty_curve)   — build practice simulator
PLANNER(student, goals, timeline)            — build personal planner
VISUALIZE(concept, method, interactivity)    — create visualizer
TRACK(student, metrics[], display)           — create progress tracker
GENERATE(domain, difficulty, count)          — generate exercises
CALIBRATE(tool, student_performance)         — adjust tool to student
```

---

## Ⅴ. STACK INTEGRATION

```
SPL (how student learns) + EDL (what system requires) = PWL (the path forward)
PWL + SPL = TSL (tools built specifically for this student on this path)

SPL  →  "This student learns best with visual + kinesthetic at moderate pace"
EDL  →  "Algebra 2 requires mastery of quadratics, functions, and proofs"
PWL  →  "Path: Algebra 2 → Pre-Calc → AP Calc → Engineering degree"
TSL  →  "Build: visual quadratic explorer + kinesthetic function grapher"
```

